<title>NORWAY: Non-Eu member Norway fulfills Maastricht criterion.</title>
<headline>Non-Eu member Norway fulfills Maastricht criterion.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1996-10-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Norway, which is not a member of the European Union, said on Friday it easily fulfilled the Maastricht criterion of a target ceiling for the deficit to be no more than three percent of gross domestic product.</p>
<p>&quot;A general government surplus of 5.1 percent of GDP is expected in 1997,&quot; the government said in unveiling its draft budget for next year.</p>
<p>&quot;This figure can be compared with the Maastricht criterion of a deficit ceiling of three percent,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>Norway rejected membership of the EU in a referendum in November 1994.</p>
<p>    --Oslo newsroom +47 22 42 50 41</p>
</text>
